# Superseded heuristic code is a crucial historical result, not current math.
c('historical','Superseded v0.1.6 backup used invented classifications and rating heuristics','The retained backup used CP thresholds excellent10/good35/inaccuracy90/mistake220,GreatFind gap120,material sacrifice2,moveAccuracy=100*exp(-(loss/220)^1.5),phase slicing,handwritten sentences and Elo-style rating heuristics. These are agent-authored approximations,not recovered proprietary algorithms. Current extension/lib/review.js instead calls shipped native CEE and carries native output; this backup must never be presented as current parity or silently omitted.', ['research/backups/review-v0.1.6.js',E+'lib/review.js'],'const T =',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Legacy external UCI wrapper remains but is not the current native review pipeline','extension/lib/engines.js defines Stockfish16.1/Torch/TorchLite workers,loader#wasm resolution,NNUE/hash/thread initialization and UCI parsing. client-math.js retains old presentation helpers and an overbroad server-only comment. Current review.js imports CeeClient rather than the external UciEngine,so presence of these files does not prove they drive production reviews.', [E+'lib/engines.js',E+'lib/client-math.js',E+'lib/review.js'],'UciEngine',verification='historical')
c('data_models','Full frontend descriptors retain service metadata omitted by old rendered schemas','The original extension/lib/descriptors.js contains base64 FileDescriptorProto blobs. The older research/extract_desc.py renderer handles messages/enums but drops service declarations and some options. This recovery decodes the authoritative original registry offline,retaining full JSON and RPC methods in registries/frontend-descriptors and rpc-services.json. This is new extraction of existing evidence,not a new network investigation.', [E+'lib/descriptors.js','research/extract_desc.py'],'DESCRIPTORS',verification='historical')
# Native website versus extension architecture.
c('architecture','Three different analysis pipelines must not be conflated','The full website Game Review request builder sends CEAC over a remote WebSocket. Quick Analysis has binary and legacy local CEE routes. The extension intercepts the full-review socket and supplies local CEE output. Local worker loading therefore does not prove that native full Game Review runs locally.',[A,Q,E+'page-hook.js',E+'lib/review.js'],'GameReviewRequest',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Production Game Review WebSocket','The saved EW.Urls table declares wss://analysis.chess.com:443/v2/game-review. x3e constructs/encodes W4e output, opens S3e socket and sends the request; C3e decodes binary responses. This is static source evidence, not a captured logged-in cloud request.',[A],'async function x3e',verification='historical')
for key,url in [('ProdServerIDLRunSearch','wss://analysis.chess.com:443/v2/run-search'),('StagingServerIDLGameReview','wss://analysis-staging.chess.com:443/v2/game-review'),('SandboxServerIDLGameReview','wss://analysis-sandbox.chess.com:443/v2/game-review'),('StagingServerIDLRunSearch','wss://analysis-staging.chess.com:443/v2/run-search'),('NewMax','wss://max-analysis.prod.chess-platform.com:443'),('StagingMax','wss://max-analysis.staging.chess-platform.com:443')]:
 c('api_network',key+' endpoint',url+' is a declared historical endpoint in EW.Urls. Protocol purpose is inferred from its table key/call sites; current reachability, authentication and authorization were not tested by this audit.',[A],key,verification='historical')
c('api_network','CEAC frame boundaries are WebSocket message boundaries','C3e decodes the ArrayBuffer directly as GameReviewResponse. extension frame() is identity normalization to Uint8Array and unframe() returns one message; there is no extra length-prefix framing in this adapter.',[A,E+'lib/protobuf.js'],'export function frame',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Handshake timeout is separate from review duration','S3e opens a WebSocket, sets binaryType=arraybuffer and uses k3e=1e4 to reject a connection not opened in ten seconds. This does not time-limit completed review computation to ten seconds.',[A],'CEAC IDL WebSocket connection timeout',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Response stream is a tagged oneof','GameReviewResponse has progress,success,failure,heartbeat,waiting_for_capacity cases. Numeric field details are in the schema registry. A progress case is not proof the engine is moving forward between frames.', ['research/proto/chesscom/ceac/v2/game_review.proto'],'message GameReviewResponse',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Request heartbeat settings','The saved W4e request uses requestOptions heartbeatIntervalSeconds5/useProgressUpdatestrue; its runSearchReq has heartbeatIntervalSeconds0 and streamResultsfalse. These are different message levels, not inconsistent settings.',[A],'heartbeatIntervalSeconds:5',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Remote run-search has a historical JSON path too','Uploaded documentation describes a plain-JSON run-search socket taking id,fen,uciMoves and returning heartbeat/waitingForCapacity. It is not the same wire representation as CEAC GameReviewResponse. Retain as historical report unless independently tied to a specific saved call site.',[P],'plain JSON',classification='unknown',verification='historical',confidence='medium')
c('api_network','Same-origin socket override is not a new public endpoint','The historical frontend references window.chesscom.analysis.ceacSocketSameOrigin. This changes routing on the client; it does not establish a currently exposed standalone local server.',[A,P],'ceacSocketSameOrigin',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','Numeric page depths select named strength','P4e maps18->Fast,22->Standard,24->Deep,26->Maximum; fallback Fast. Strength enum is1/2/3/4. A depth menu selection is not a guarantee the engine searches every position to that exact depth.',[A,'research/proto/chesscom/engine/v1/strength.proto'],'function P4e',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','Torch Human engine selection is feature-gated','A4e checks web_analysis_torch_human_v2. With the flag, Stockfish16 selection yields SF16_1_NNUE, other selection yields TORCH_HUMAN; without it, SF16_1_NNUE. W4e sets useGameStateCache false for TORCH_HUMAN. The causal reason for disabling cache is not proved by that expression.',[A],'function A4e',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','Report-card entitlement modifies request options','M4e combines game_review_platinum_report_card and af(); af checks analysis.hasUnlimitedReview and non-Diamond state. W4e carries reportCardEntitled/includeTrainTakeaways/canAccessLockedTakeaways. Client flags do not establish a server authorization bypass.',[A,P],'function M4e',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','Displayed Game Rating is not the WDL model','The report-card adapter copies native effectiveRating/gameRatingV2. The WDL/confidence-band arithmetic affects prose/bands, not a proven rating-generation algorithm. An old claim that no shipped file can calculate rating is superseded by the executable CEE WASM producing effectiveRating locally.',[A,E+'lib/review.js',P],'gameRatingV2',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','CAPS2 schema does not establish its mathematical dependency','AccuracyAlgorithm includes CAPS2; ColorAccuracy carries accuracy_overall and avg_centipawn_loss. Coexistence of these fields does NOT prove accuracy is a simple transform of average centipawn loss, nor reveal the exact native algorithm. Preserve older stronger claims as unverified.',[P,'research/proto/chesscom/explanation_engine/v1/accuracy.proto'],'CAPS2',classification='inference',verification='partially verified',confidence='high',why='The schema declaration is direct; the limitation is logical: fields alone do not establish causation.')
c('business_logic','WDL model constants preserved without conflating their role','Historical document records arctan win/loss coefficients0.20773843,2.49085889,2.47841945 and0.20720905,2.49626837,2.48220286; draw term uses exp and normalization w+l+d. Full exact formula and computed tables remain preserved in original document blocks, not substituted for native Game Rating.',[P,A],'0.20773843',verification='historical')
c('business_logic','Rating confidence-band inverse-logistic formula','Historical source describes log(1/probability-1)/(0.004*((0.0685*rating-12)/100))/100, with rating=max(playerElos), fallback2000. It is used for pawn-score prose bands, not headline rating. The full five-band thresholds and ten downgrade sentence keys are preserved in documentary blocks.',[P,A],'0.0685',verification='historical')
c('data_models','Compact CEE classification enum differs from legacy analysis enum','chesscom.explanation_engine.v1.MoveClassification uses Mistake8,Blunder9,Missed10,Forced11,Tricky20. chesscom.analysis.v1.MoveClassification uses Mistake11,Blunder15,Forced19,Miss20 and phase splits. Do not decode CEE output using the legacy32-value table.', ['research/proto/chesscom/explanation_engine/v1/move_classification.proto','research/proto/chesscom/analysis/v1/move_classifications.proto',P],'MOVE_CLASSIFICATION_MISTAKE',verification='historical')
c('data_models','MoveClassificationVersion numeric names','CEE version UNSPECIFIED0,V2=1,V3=2. Sweep labels such as class-v2/ClassificationV3 must be interpreted through actual config fields, not their informal label; a "class0" omitted setting is not an explicit algorithm-version0 run.', ['research/proto/chesscom/explanation_engine/v1/move_classification.proto','research/refinement/sweep.mjs'],'MoveClassificationVersion',verification='historical')
c('data_models','White-point-of-view scores and board-bar pawn scores','Native chess Score can encode score_centipawns_white or mate cases. UI conversion divides CP by100. Legacy evaluation-bar payload uses pawns and White POV; UCI side-to-move scores must be normalized by the wrapper. Always preserve the namespace/unit rather than assuming all score fields have identical meaning.',[P,B,E+'lib/protobuf.js'],'score_centipawns_white',verification='historical')
c('data_models','Skills hash prerequisites do not prove cryptographic security','Frontend logs say CEE needs White user ID,Black user ID,game ID to sign validationHash and warns it will be empty otherwise. The log wording and schema support dependency/intent, not an independently assessed signature algorithm, server validation behavior, or guaranteed skill credit.',[A,P],'validationHash',verification='historical')
c('data_models','Both native and frontend metadata versions are retained','CEE startup banner1.130.285 and review metadata1.211.5 were recorded in different contexts. They may refer to packaging/API metadata versus internal engine build. Do not overwrite one with the other or conclude a contradiction without a version mapping.', ['research/refinement/uci-options.txt','research/doting-cee-baseline.json',H],'1.130.285',classification='inference',verification='partially verified',confidence='medium')
