c('frontend','Quick Analysis has a dedicated lazy client','The example game page package is play2026.11.4. Static dependency tracing reaches client.e0da4c65.BIjoPk3wAJ.chunk.js. Its store extension.quick-analysis keeps resultsMap,engine,evaluationEngines,cee,preloadAssetsPromise,pendingBrilliantVerifications. Package imports are code observations, not proof all clients initialize for every session.',[Q,'research/refinement/live-chunks/shared.b9742e37.Cgvw1kitOr.chunk.js'],'extension.quick-analysis',verification='historical')
c('frontend','Quick Analysis binary-interface gate','An() tests web_quick_analysis_cee_binary_interface. The binary path calls createNewGame then getGameReview; the old path initializes CEE plus separate evaluation engines and fetches analysis.',[Q],'web_quick_analysis_cee_binary_interface',verification='historical')
c('frontend','Quick Analysis binary search settings','G defines defaultDepth10,multiPv2. $i creates NewGame with searchSettings/searchParameters depthLimit10,numLines2. Coach mode selects classificationV3 and userColor; no-coach mode selects V2. These are not the named Torch Human+Fast whole-review settings.',[Q],'defaultDepth:10',verification='historical')
c('frontend','Legacy Quick Analysis supplies external evaluations','lr returns action analysis,evals,moves,startFen,variant,WhiteElo,BlackElo,ClassificationV3true,DoProgressUpdatestrue,uciCommands. hr builds evaluation workers from engine asset paths, and br/xr distribute position searches. This is separate from the CEE internal search route.',[Q],'ClassificationV3:!0',verification='historical')
c('frontend','Quick Analysis worker parallelism derives from device concurrency','kr uses navigator.hardwareConcurrency fallback1, a special condition returning1, otherwise max(floor(concurrency/2)-1,1). This worker-count policy is distinct from sequential research trials that avoid sandbox OOM.',[Q],'function kr()',verification='historical')
c('api_network','Brilliant verification can modify a local tally afterward','The Quick Analysis client creates a BrilliantVerificationService using /rpc/ceac, collects brilliant move indices, sends game metadata,selected engine and Fast searchSettings, then replaces the relevant brilliant count with returned classifications. This is declared behavior, not a captured RPC. It prevents assuming the final post-game card is wholly local.',[Q],'/rpc/ceac',verification='historical')
c('frontend','Binary debug switch has initialization requirements','Ri checks location.search for logBIMessages. Ni creates binary client with a Pi logger when enabled; Pi exposes window.chesscom.getCeeBinaryInterfaceLogs. This function does not have to exist before that client initializes or in another frame/isolated world.',[Q],'function Ri()',verification='historical')
c('historical','User debug-console exception did not establish an engine failure','The user ran window.chesscom.getCeeBinaryInterfaceLogs() and got TypeError reading the method because window.chesscom was undefined. No exact execution context or cause was established; do not claim the correct frame selection was tested.',[H],'getCeeBinaryInterfaceLogs()',verification='historical',confidence='high',why='Directly available user report in the current conversation; cause remains unknown.')
c('frontend','CEE asset version and SIMD selection are flag-dependent','Saved live-shared eager source chooses R2 assets when explanation_engine_r2 is enabled outside dev/test; WJ selects default package1.130.285 or staff-config version/fallback1.130.254. explanation_engine_no_simd and WebAssembly SIMD validation choose default/no-simd. Legacy fallback uses bundles/app/js/vendor/explanation-engine or -staff.', ['research/refinement/live-shared.eager.js'],'function act()',verification='historical')
