# Local worker/API internals.
c('local_engine','CEE JS is a loader/bridge, WASM contains native machinery','The loader is about129KB and exposes Emscripten/native CEE APIs. WASM strings and extracted descriptors include TorchHuman,Maia,torch_search_mode,PVtrees and native source paths. Presence of strings proves embedded machinery, not that every model/feature is usable or a separate Torch Human binary exists.', [E+'engines/cee/explanation-engine.js',E+'engines/cee/explanation-engine.wasm'],'TorchHuman',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Human mode requires a Torch engine','Native error string includes "is not a Torch engine, and Torch Human mode requires one". This is a requirement check in the shipped binary; it does not make Stockfish a Human engine or document all accepted engine-instance IDs.',[E+'engines/cee/explanation-engine.wasm'],'Torch Human mode requires one',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Local human request changes actual UCI command shape','Feature29 RunSearch1000nodes with torchSearchMode.mode.case=human produced go nodes1000 pvtrees with splitDepthLimit6,splitWidthLimit2,allowedExcessWidth2,rating2100,max_allowed_cp_margin100,ep_loss_margin0.02. Control used searchmoves. This is execution evidence that the flag is not ignored, not proof of exact server settings.', ['research/refinement/probe-human-decoded-log.txt','research/refinement/probe-normal-decoded-log.txt'],'pvtrees',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Offline local Human probe completed','Stored probe-human-offline.json records progress1,+18cp,depth5,nodes859,underlying engine11 and engine log Torch master-20260925-87ee25a. The runner replaces fetch with a rejecting function and records attempts; none was recorded. This is a Node-wrapper local WASM test, not a Chrome UI/cloud-network trace.', ['research/refinement/results/probe-human-offline.json','research/refinement/human-probe.mjs'],'Torch master-',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Offline normal control completed','Stored normal control records+17cp,depth6,nodes717,progress1,engine11, same Torch build. Thus engine11 does not by itself diagnose whether human search logic ran.', ['research/refinement/results/probe-normal-offline.json','research/refinement/results/probe-human-offline.json'],'"depth": 6',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Human underlying enum11 and CEAC requested enum12 are different layers','Website CEAC Engine.TORCH_HUMAN is12; native search still reports underlying Torch11 when human mode runs. Earlier ID-only inference was too strict. This does not mean all ordinary CEE11 reviews automatically used human mode.',[H,'research/refinement/results/probe-human-offline.json',A],'engine11',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Feature29/79/54/288 do not behave interchangeably','Successful RunSearch29 and GetGameReviewEvaluations79 human paths coexist with timed-out InternalFeatureRunPvTrees288 and aborted EvaluateGame54, including a normal control. A timeout or assertion in one interface does not prove all local human support is absent.', ['research/refinement/results/comparison-human.json','research/refinement/results/probe-pvtree-human.json','research/refinement/results/normalized-evaluate-normal.json'],'trial timeout',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Native mode incompatibility strings','WASM says torch_search_mode.human is incompatible with reduce_nodes_on_successive_multisearch_searches; that reduction also requires multisearch without pvtrees and a nodes-only limit. Treat these as declared native validation constraints, not newly tested every-branch behavior.',[E+'engines/cee/explanation-engine.wasm'],'torch_search_mode.human is incompatible',verification='historical')
c('local_engine','Engine-instance options are not engine enum IDs','Native v1alpha EngineInstanceOptions carries binary_path,type,web_worker.script_url; InitEnginePool returns instance.id,pid. An engine_id parameter may refer to an instance rather than enum11/12. Presence alone does not establish a supported browser external-engine configuration.', ['research/refinement/wasm-descriptors/chesscom_explanation_engine_v1alpha_engine_instance_options.proto.txt'],'binary_path',classification='inference',verification='partially verified',confidence='medium')
c('local_engine','CEE export JS arity is uninformative about native signature','export-signatures.json records CEE_Init0 and CEE_InitWithOpts0 JS arity. InitWithOptsCall descriptor has n_async_task_processors and engine_pool_size. Arity0 is not proof the native API takes no options or provides a TorchHuman toggle.', ['research/refinement/export-signatures.json','research/refinement/torch-human-evidence.txt'],'CEE_Init',verification='historical')
c('extension','Main-world hook and isolated bridge have distinct responsibilities','Manifest injects page-hook.js at document_start in MAIN across matching frames; bridge.js uses isolated content context. Page hook intercepts review sockets and patches client launch flags; bridge moves data to service-worker/offscreen. They are not website-native scripts.', [E+'manifest.json',E+'page-hook.js',E+'bridge.js'],'"world": "MAIN"')
c('extension','Quota launch checks are canCreate and locked, not just unlimited review','Historical quota fix patches local analysis permission flags before the page snapshots them, preserving original PGN/config and handling later assignments or replacement objects. It is a local presentation/transport intervention; it does not change server membership,quota,library permissions or cloud storage.', [E+'page-hook.js',E+'test/quota-test.mjs','QUOTA-FIX-INSTALL.txt'],'canCreate')
c('extension','WebSocket brand-check regression is explicit','Native prototype binaryType accessors reject unbranded receivers. The hook harness proves bare objects throw Illegal invocation, then exercises intercepted constructor,open,send,close,retry and passthrough with brand checks. This explains older superficially passing fake-socket tests being inadequate.', [E+'test/hook-test.mjs',E+'page-hook.js'],'Illegal invocation')
c('extension','Only Game Review sockets loop back locally','Hook route predicate intercepts configured CEAC game-review URLs, including same-origin variation; other sockets pass through native WebSocket. It handles ArrayBuffer binary frames and retains instanceof behavior. This is not a general network proxy.',[E+'page-hook.js',E+'test/hook-test.mjs'],'passthrough')
c('extension','Chrome runtime messaging needs base64 for binary','bridge.js comments and functions document JSON serialization turning ArrayBuffer into{}. Binary data crosses chrome.runtime Port as base64 then converts back to bytes for window.postMessage/socket events. Encoding uses0x8000 chunks to avoid huge apply calls.',[E+'bridge.js',E+'offscreen.js'],'B64_CHUNK')
c('extension','Offscreen host dials out to avoid lost initial ports','Offscreen module connects as engine after module graph initialization; SW binds/queues until ready rather than dialing into an unregistered listener. SW engine-bind timeout15seconds; it creates offscreen.html for WORKERS. Session keys route frames to content ports.', [E+'service-worker.js',E+'offscreen.js'],'ENGINE_BIND_TIMEOUT_MS')
c('extension','Service-worker keepalive and computation progress are separate','bridge sends ping every20000ms, service-worker handles port lifecycle, and offscreen sends progress keepalives. These are not engine work completion. SW lifecycle behavior should not be inferred solely from page percentage.',[E+'bridge.js',E+'service-worker.js',E+'offscreen.js'],'20000')
c('extension','CEE API client serializes no-request-ID calls','CeeClient maintains tail,pending,timer; CEE_Run accepts message.proto updates until is_final; logs/UCI notifications are not ordinary API replies. Worker errors fail and terminate the client. Default timeout240000ms; feature handles disposed in finally and worker disposed at review end.', [E+'lib/cee.js'],'this.tail')
c('extension','Native review adapter merges CEAC search settings','newGameRequest merges runSearchReq search into NewGame settings, supports PGN or positionWithMoves fallback,defaults Fast and localeen_US. It forwards explicit result metadata and validates review move count against native playedLine.',[E+'lib/review.js'],'function newGameRequest')
c('extension','Legacy effectiveRating alias is transparent, not verified V2 prediction','If CEE omits gameRatingV2, adapter copies effectiveRating to that optional field so current UI can display it, while diagnostics retain ratingSources. This is compatibility aliasing, not proof native V2 generation or a guessed curve.',[E+'lib/review.js'],'card.gameRatingV2 = card.effectiveRating')
c('extension','Native speech hashes and arrows survive the adapter','reviewStats counts speechSentences,audioHashes,boardMarkings and fragment arrows; returned GameReview retains native speech text/hash,explainLine,alternatives,opening,result and PGN. Counts alone do not prove a selected coach or audio fetch played correctly; user confirmation is separate.',[E+'lib/review.js','research/browser-cee-test.json'],'audioHashes')
c('extension','Manifest permissions and CSP belong to extension, not website','Manifest minimumChrome116,permissionoffscreen,script-src self wasm-unsafe-eval/object-src self,service worker and engine web_accessible_resources. Do not report this as the live Chess.com HTTP CSP, CORS policy, or security-header audit.',[E+'manifest.json'],'content_security_policy')
c('extension','Update ZIPs are overlays, not standalone installers','v0.1.6/0.1.8/0.1.9 ZIPs contain selected changed files and depend on existing engine/lib/bridge/SW assets. Delete-and-replace of the entire extension directory can break installation. Reload extension and refresh tabs after overlay.',[E+'README.md','QUOTA-FIX-INSTALL.txt'],'not a standalone')
c('extension','Hook VERSION0.1.6 is retained with manifest0.1.9','page-hook internal VERSION stays0.1.6 to identify core quota/socket code; manifest is0.1.9. Badge flagfalse suppresses DOM creation; this version mismatch alone does not mean an update failed.',[E+'page-hook.js',E+'manifest.json'],'SHOW_DEBUG_BADGE')
c('progress','Original coarse progress was0/2/100, not a hidden-card regression','v0.1.7 offscreen repeated the last native milestone every4seconds. User initially reported a stall at0.019999999552965164 then clarified review succeeded and only percentage was wrong. There was no confirmed full review failure caused by hiding the badge.',[H,'chess-local-review-v0.1.7-cee-update.zip!/offscreen.js'],'0.019999999552965164',verification='historical')
c('progress','v0.1.9 progress uses real local successful-duration samples','ReviewProgressEstimator retains last40valid samples, groups by exact searchKey,selects up to7nearest lengths by absolute log position ratio,scales each duration by(currentPlies+1)/(samplePlies+1),then takes median. No stock timing constant trains a first-run estimate.',[E+'lib/progress.js'],'Math.abs(Math.log')
c('progress','First matching review is calibration, not smooth estimated progress','begin returns expectedMsnull without matching history; progress returnsnull. Original coarse milestones remain for that first review/strength. Later successful reviews train history. This deliberate limitation must be disclosed during installation.',[E+'lib/progress.js',E+'README.md'],'expectedMs')
c('progress','Estimated percentage is time-based and caps below completion','progress=min(0.95,0.02+0.93*elapsed/expectedMs). Offscreen ticks each1000ms,uses max to prevent backward movement and only reaches1when native result exists. At/after predicted duration it holds95%; not a position-completion counter or guaranteed ETA.',[E+'lib/progress.js',E+'offscreen.js'],'0.93')
c('progress','History persistence excludes personal game contents','localStorage key clr.review-timings.cee-1.130.285.pipeline1 stores plies,searchKey,durationMs only; no PGN/handle. Storage errors fall back to in-memory model. Failed/cancelled reviews do not complete/train samples. This is extension-local storage, not Chess.com page localStorage.',[E+'offscreen.js',E+'lib/progress.js'],'clr.review-timings')
c('progress','Progress metadata callback is presentation-only','buildGameReview calls onWorkload after native NewGame with actual playedLine count and serialized search settings. It does not pre-search positions or change the CEE review call. Progress tests exercise mocked offscreen clock/history/failure/cancellation and real native review regression separately.',[E+'lib/review.js',E+'test/progress-test.mjs'],'onWorkload')
